      "bottomRightX": 407,
      "bottomRightY": 88,
      "content": "# Language review 9",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 87,
      "topLeftY": 104,
      "bottomRightX": 225,
      "bottomRightY": 122,
      "content": "### 1 *Modal verbs - 1*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 136,
      "bottomRightX": 515,
      "bottomRightY": 170,
      "content": "Modal verbs are not used on their own. They are used with other verbs to express different meanings.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 170,
      "bottomRightX": 245,
      "bottomRightY": 187,
      "content": "- Degrees of possibility",
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 187,
      "bottomRightX": 202,
      "bottomRightY": 201,
      "content": "You are not certain.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 208,
      "bottomRightX": 442,
      "bottomRightY": 226,
      "content": "**Example:** It may (not)/might (not) could be a toothbrush.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 238,
      "bottomRightX": 180,
      "bottomRightY": 254,
      "content": "You are certain.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 261,
      "bottomRightX": 373,
      "bottomRightY": 294,
      "content": "**Examples:** (Positive) I must be a toothbrush.\n(Negative) I can't be a toothbrush.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 294,
      "bottomRightX": 551,
      "bottomRightY": 328,
      "content": "**Note:** *Must not (mustn't)* can only be used when you want to tell somebody that they are not allowed to do something.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 328,
      "bottomRightX": 441,
      "bottomRightY": 345,
      "content": "**Example:** You must not look at your books during an exam.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 361,
      "bottomRightX": 274,
      "bottomRightY": 460,
      "content": "- Ability\n  *can/cannot* refers to the present\n  *could (not)* is used\n  - to refer to the past\n  - after *wish*\n  - in conditional sentences",
      "type": "list"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 491,
      "bottomRightX": 429,
      "bottomRightY": 559,
      "content": "**Examples:** I can /cannot swim.\nI could (not) swim when I was six.\nI wish I could swim.\nIf I lived near the sea, I could learn to swim.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 559,
      "bottomRightX": 348,
      "bottomRightY": 575,
      "content": "**Note:** You can use **be able to** instead of **can**.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 575,
      "bottomRightX": 326,
      "bottomRightY": 609,
      "content": "**Examples:** I am able to swim.\nI wish I was able to swim.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 87,
      "topLeftY": 637,
      "bottomRightX": 320,
      "bottomRightY": 655,
      "content": "### 2 *'Sense' verbs + object + verb*",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 87,
      "topLeftY": 667,
      "bottomRightX": 570,
      "bottomRightY": 718,
      "content": "Some sense verbs are followed by the *-ing* form. This emphasizes the action as continuous and is often used for setting the scene (see Language review 4). When followed by the infinitive, this emphasizes that the action is completed.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 730,
      "bottomRightX": 500,
      "bottomRightY": 797,
      "content": "**Example:** I saw/heard/watched the goats come down the street.\n(And later told the farmer what I saw/heard, etc.)\nI saw/heard/watched the goats coming down the street.\n(And tried to stop them coming into the garden.)",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 87,
      "topLeftY": 808,
      "bottomRightX": 416,
      "bottomRightY": 825,
      "content": "**Find examples of this language in the texts.**",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 87,
      "topLeftY": 844,
      "bottomRightX": 414,
      "bottomRightY": 862,
      "content": "**Now do activities A and B in the Workbook.**",
      "type": "text"
    },
